From ab4f505181e13699417f251729e7c09053c39be0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:23:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the player information: what the TV declares, the
 overview with air

System page:
 - beside the connection to the TV, what the TV declares in its EDID
   (41909 to 41923): its HDR formats, Dolby Vision, the VRR range, the
   fastest FRL, ALLM, QMS and FreeSync; "Not declared" where it says
   none, "Not read from the TV" without an EDID;
 - the playback goes under the connection, and the versions under what
   the TV declares.

Overview: where no row says how HDR10 is adapted to the TV (most videos),
the page takes the room that row would take: the strip lower, its cards
taller with their lines further apart, and the rows under them higher and
further from the cards. Where that row is there, in up to three lines,
the page is as it was. The tallest column of each layout fits in the
frame at its most, in the four languages (skin_check.py).

The frame keeps its height (820). The Dolby Vision page, the longest, has
its three columns at 396, 420 and 393 of 420 px at their most: on the
left, in Spanish and with the longest values, the profile, the maps of
the composer and the transport take two lines each. The three rows of
its last 10 s take least where they are, under the levels; on the left
they would make the frame 66 px higher.

The row "Audio stream" (Kodi's 460) that fcea427 left out of the sound
out of the Audio page said what the row "Sample format" (31815) of the
sound of the film says: Player.Process(audiobitspersample) and
Player.Process(audiosamplerate) are CDataCacheCore's
GetAudioBitsPerSample() and GetAudioSampleRate() (PlayerGUIInfo.cpp),
which PublishPlayerInfo() publishes for that row as hades.audio.srcbits
and hades.audio.srcrate (in kHz, as the rest of the page). Its "Audio
channels" (31605) was Player.Process(audiochannels), the label of the
row "Layout" (31814) of the film.

system/hades made again.
